{
  "name": "text that is no message of the profile ends the connection as a protocol error, from a consumer and from the machine",
  "layer": "session",
  "replaces": "session/go/sessiontest and session/ts/src/conformance.ts, across the wire",
  "description": "A session speaks the profile in JSON text. Text that is no message of it — no JSON at all, an object with a member named twice, content after the object — is a protocol error, 1002, under a reason naming what was wrong with the frame, where a frame of the wrong kind is unsupported data. The reasons are a closed set and the same in both languages, a consumer reading one off the close being unable to ask which runtime wrote the relay. Either side may send such text: a consumer's ends its own connection and leaves the session standing, the machine's ends the session and every consumer with it.",
  "needs": [
    "lazy",
    "peer",
    "pipe",
    "seam",
    "session",
    "tunnel"
  ],
  "mirror": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "on": "runner",
      "op": "pair.peers",
      "args": {
        "server": "a"
      },
      "bind": {
        "server": "pa",
        "client": "pb"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.over",
      "args": {
        "on": "$pa"
      },
      "bind": "carrier_a"
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "tunnel.over",
      "args": {
        "on": "$pb"
      },
      "bind": "carrier_b"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "conn.pipe",
      "args": {
        "consume": "lazy"
      },
      "bind": {
        "a": "pipe_near",
        "b": "pipe_far"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "peer.over",
      "args": {
        "on": "$pipe_near",
        "role": "client"
      },
      "bind": "near"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "peer.over",
      "args": {
        "on": "$pipe_far",
        "role": "server"
      },
      "bind": "far"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.over",
      "args": {
        "on": "$near"
      },
      "bind": "tunnel_near"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.over",
      "args": {
        "on": "$far"
      },
      "bind": "tunnel_far"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.open",
      "args": {
        "on": "$tunnel_far",
        "family": "probe",
        "consume": "eager"
      },
      "bind": "machine"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.accept",
      "args": {
        "on": "$tunnel_near",
        "consume": "lazy"
      },
      "bind": "up"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "session.new",
      "bind": "reg"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "session.bind",
      "args": {
        "on": "$reg",
        "session": "s",
        "channel": "$up",
        "governance": {
          "decides": [
            "echo"
          ],
          "asks": [
            "reverse"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "tunnel.open",
      "args": {
        "on": "$carrier_b",
        "family": "probe",
        "consume": "eager"
      },
      "bind": "one"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.accept",
      "args": {
        "on": "$carrier_a",
        "consume": "lazy"
      },
      "bind": {
        "handle": "ch_one"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "session.attach",
      "args": {
        "on": "$reg",
        "session": "s",
        "channel": "$ch_one",
        "role": "participant",
        "origin": "one",
        "after": 0
      },
      "bind": "att_one"
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "tunnel.open",
      "args": {
        "on": "$carrier_b",
        "family": "probe",
        "consume": "eager"
      },
      "bind": "two"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.accept",
      "args": {
        "on": "$carrier_a",
        "consume": "lazy"
      },
      "bind": {
        "handle": "ch_two"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "session.attach",
      "args": {
        "on": "$reg",
        "session": "s",
        "channel": "$ch_two",
        "role": "observer",
        "origin": "watcher",
        "after": 0
      },
      "bind": "att_watcher"
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "tunnel.open",
      "args": {
        "on": "$carrier_b",
        "family": "probe",
        "consume": "eager"
      },
      "bind": "three"
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "tunnel.accept",
      "args": {
        "on": "$carrier_a",
        "consume": "lazy"
      },
      "bind": {
        "handle": "ch_three"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "session.attach",
      "args": {
        "on": "$reg",
        "session": "s",
        "channel": "$ch_three",
        "role": "participant",
        "origin": "three",
        "after": 0
      },
      "bind": "att_three"
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.receive",
      "args": {
        "on": "$two"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "{\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"event\",\"event\":\"session.control\",\"data\":{\"holder\":null}}"
      },
      "note": "Who holds control is the first frame on a consumer's connection, taken here so that the quiet below reads a connection with nothing on it."
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.send",
      "args": {
        "on": "$one",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "not json"
      },
      "note": "Text is where a message of the profile would be, so what is wrong is the message and not the frame: a protocol error under the reason naming the fault."
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.await_close",
      "args": {
        "on": "$one"
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": 1002,
        "reason": "a session frame must be a JSON object"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.receive",
      "args": {
        "on": "$two",
        "within_ms": 250
      },
      "expect_error": {
        "code": "timeout"
      },
      "note": "The session stands: the consumer that sent the frame is the only one ended by it."
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.send",
      "args": {
        "on": "$three",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "{\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"event\",\"event\":\"changed\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"x\",\"count\":1}} {}"
      },
      "note": "A second of the three reasons, from a second consumer: one object of the profile and another after it is no message either."
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.await_close",
      "args": {
        "on": "$three"
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": 1002,
        "reason": "invalid trailing session frame content"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "conn.send",
      "args": {
        "on": "$machine",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "{\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"event\",\"event\":\"changed\",\"data\":{\"text\":\"still here\",\"count\":1}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.receive",
      "args": {
        "on": "$two"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "$regex:\"event\":\"changed\""
      },
      "note": "And it goes on routing."
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.receive",
      "args": {
        "on": "$two"
      },
      "expect": {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "$regex:\"event\":\"session.cursor\""
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "conn.send",
      "args": {
        "on": "$machine",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "{\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"request\",\"id\":\"s:1\",\"id\":\"s:2\",\"method\":\"reverse\",\"params\":{\"text\":\"x\",\"count\":1}}"
      },
      "note": "The machine's own ends the session, and every consumer with it, under the code and the reason its own fault carries."
    },
    {
      "on": "b",
      "op": "conn.await_close",
      "args": {
        "on": "$two"
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": 1002,
        "reason": "duplicate session frame member \"id\""
      }
    },
    {
      "on": "a",
      "op": "conn.await_close",
      "args": {
        "on": "$machine"
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": 1002,
        "reason": "duplicate session frame member \"id\""
      }
    }
  ]
}
